 "key_sub": "Divide by multiplying top and bottom by the conjugate.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How it works</h2><ul><li><i>i</i> = √−1, so <i>i</i>² = −1, <i>i</i>³ = −<i>i</i>, <i>i</i>⁴ = 1. Powers of <i>i</i> repeat every 4.</li><li>z = a + <i>i</i>b has real part a and imaginary part b. Two complex numbers are equal when both parts are equal.</li><li>Conjugate z̄ = a − <i>i</i>b; modulus |z| = √(a² + b²); z z̄ = |z|²; z<sup>−1</sup> = z̄ ÷ |z|².</li><li>For a<i>x</i>² + b<i>x</i> + c = 0 with D = b² − 4ac &lt; 0, <i>x</i> = (−b ± <i>i</i>√−D) ÷ 2a.</li></ul><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Express (3 + 2<i>i</i>) ÷ (1 − <i>i</i>) in the form a + <i>i</i>b.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>Multiply top and bottom by 1 + <i>i</i></p><p class='sn-ex-s'>(3 + 2<i>i</i>)(1 + <i>i</i>) = 1 + 5<i>i</i>; (1 − <i>i</i>)(1 + <i>i</i>) = 2</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 1/2 + (5/2)<i>i</i></p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><ul><li>Writing √−4 · √−9 = √36 = 6 (it is −6).</li><li>Giving the imaginary part as 3<i>i</i> instead of 3.</li><li>Taking |3 + 4<i>i</i>| = 7.</li></ul>",
